sequenceDiagram
    actor Client
    participant MW as Middlewares<br/>(cors, helmet, rate-limit)
    participant Route as Router (/api/v1)
    participant Auth as apiKeyAuth<br/>(X-API-Key)
    participant Val as Validation middleware<br/>(Yup)
    participant Ctrl as Controller
    participant UC as Use Case
    participant Repo as PostgresProductRepository
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant Err as handlingErrors

    Client->>MW: HTTP request
    alt rate limit exceeded
        MW-->>Client: 429 Too Many Requests
    else within limit
        MW->>Route: forward request
        Route->>Auth: check X-API-Key header
        alt missing or invalid key
            Auth->>Err: throw AppError(401, Unauthorized)
            Err-->>Client: 401 JSON {message, type}
        else key valid
            Auth->>Val: validate body / params / query
            alt validation fails
                Val->>Err: throw AppError(400, VALIDATION_FAILED)
                Err-->>Client: 400 JSON {message, type}
            else valid
                Val->>Ctrl: next()
                Ctrl->>UC: execute(dto)
                UC->>Repo: create / update / find / remove
                Repo->>PG: read / write (MVCC, concurrent-safe)
                PG-->>Repo: rows
                alt not found (404) or conflict (409)
                    Repo->>Err: throw AppError(code, type)
                    Err-->>Client: error JSON {message, type}
                else success
                    Repo-->>UC: result
                    UC-->>Ctrl: result
                    Ctrl-->>Client: 200 / 201 JSON
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Ctrl,Repo: Any unhandled (non-AppError) exception<br/>is caught by express-async-errors<br/>and routed to handlingErrors → 500<br/>(stack trace hidden when NODE_ENV=production)
